# Upstream-owned files the fork changes on purpose (scripts/fork/verify-sync.sh). The list grows with the fork: the fork may differ
# from upstream wherever it is better. Upstream is an imported source, nothing here is offered back. A replayed upstream change to
# one of these files that touches the same lines stops the replay (docs/fork/KEEPING-IN-SYNC.md, "Who wins").
README.md
# Test speed: the function table of a test engine is collected once per thread and copied (docs/fork/CI.md, "Upstream offers").
crates/engine-core/src/engine.rs  # Engine::new_untyped copies a per-thread template in test builds
# Test speed (docs/fork/CI.md, "Upstream offers"): each is a small, separable change in the differential harness.
crates/engine-core/src/typed/diff.rs  # a case runs under its second control word only when the first run read or loaded the word
crates/engine-core/src/x87.rs  # test builds note that the control word was read or loaded (nothing in a production build)
crates/engine-core/src/units/crt.rs  # FSTCW's read through the thread block is noted too (test builds)
# Native Linux build (docs/fork/LINUX.md): each change is cfg-gated or additive; Windows code is unchanged.
crates/engine-platform/Cargo.toml  # d3d9-wgpu as a dependency on every target (was Windows only)
crates/engine-platform/src/d3d9device.rs  # the argument-word trait is built on Windows only (reserved area: no call site touched)
crates/engine-platform/src/d3d9resource.rs  # its import of that trait is Windows only (reserved area: no call site touched)
crates/engine-platform/src/d3dx.rs  # an unused binding off Windows
crates/engine-platform/src/files.rs  # a warning-only attribute and a test constant off Windows
crates/d3d9-wgpu/src/loading.rs  # the output capture's pipe list is built on Windows only
# Linux build, found by verify-sync.sh in the Pipeline: each is a small cfg-gated change.
crates/host/src/cell_offsets.rs  # the plugin path goes through files::real_path (a Linux path is not the game's backslash path)
crates/d3d9-wgpu/tests/frame.rs  # three 8x multisampling tests are ignored off Windows (lavapipe offers 4x at most; nv-linux#189)
